    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0117" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg29"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G/279: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-13T19:00:00-05:00">October 13, 1933—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>79. You may discreetly ask the Minister of Foreign Affairs whether, in view of
                    the continuance of the conditions that figured in decision in May, 1932, to
                    postpone the Conference,<anchor n="31" xml:id="d31-f1"/> he does not believe
                    that it would be of interest to the other American nations to have his views (as
                    set forth in your telegram No. 86, October 4, 1 p.m.) brought to their
                    attention.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
